Jones was never expected to succeed .. as the name suggests, this
was simply a way to pass the time.  Nonetheless, he actually ascended
while committing 5 major mistakes.

Some log extracts:

Turn 704 Things started to look up for Mr. Jones as he finds gauntlets
of power. Although this loses him supernatural abilities unless he
takes
them off, it doubles his carrying capacity and allows him to hit hard,
so we keep 'em.

Turn 1897 - Arrive in minetown to find TWO bones pile - a previous
barbarian who had been beaten to death by a Gnome King. Little of
interest.
However, the SECOND bones in front of a shop .. a wizard by the name
of Goldsteing. Found the shopkeeper outside (Mr. Nosnehpets) wandering
outside. "Oh, hello! I was looking for goldstein!"

My, what an exciting life he must have
lead.

Evidently the previous character had accidentally blasted the shop
door.  and had run but not made it. His ghost had fought hard, but had
left a nice
pile including  magicbane, a silver dragon scale mail
and a cloak of magic resistance.   Nonetheless, it was a sobering
reminder that your equipment can't keep you safe.  I believe the
caution
this caused kept me alive for the rest of the game.  Meanwhile, my pet
cat (Xena) seems to have taken on a rock troll or such like and lost.
I attempted to tame 3 more pets, but they all got killed, and two
of them (including a red naga I got from a figurine) went feral and
I killed them myself.

Turn 6340 - Major screwup number 1. Engrave with a marble wand and
